          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Let the roots of ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "3x^2+6x-1=0",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " be ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\alpha",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\beta",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". Find the following.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p43-q34-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha^2+\\beta^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{14}{3}$",
          "worked": "The sum and product of roots are $\\alpha+\\beta=-2$ and $\\alpha\\beta=-\\dfrac13$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha^2+\\beta^2&=(\\alpha+\\beta)^2-2\\alpha\\beta\\\\\\alpha^2+\\beta^2&=(-2)^2-2\\left(-\\frac13\\right)\\\\\\alpha^2+\\beta^2&=\\frac{14}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-q34-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\alpha}{\\beta}+\\dfrac{\\beta}{\\alpha}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-14$",
          "worked": "Using $\\alpha^2+\\beta^2=\\dfrac{14}{3}$ and $\\alpha\\beta=-\\dfrac13$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\alpha}{\\beta}+\\frac{\\beta}{\\alpha}&=\\frac{\\alpha^2+\\beta^2}{\\alpha\\beta}\\\\\\frac{\\alpha}{\\beta}+\\frac{\\beta}{\\alpha}&=\\frac{14/3}{-1/3}\\\\\\frac{\\alpha}{\\beta}+\\frac{\\beta}{\\alpha}&=-14\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-q34-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(2-\\alpha)(2-\\beta)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{23}{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(2-\\alpha)(2-\\beta)&=4-2(\\alpha+\\beta)+\\alpha\\beta\\\\(2-\\alpha)(2-\\beta)&=4-2(-2)-\\frac13\\\\(2-\\alpha)(2-\\beta)&=\\frac{23}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-q34-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha^3+\\beta^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p43-q34-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "-10",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p43-q34-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Multiply each root's quadratic equation by that root, then add.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Since $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ satisfy the quadratic, multiplying their equations by $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ respectively gives\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\alpha^3+6\\alpha^2-\\alpha&=0\\\\3\\beta^3+6\\beta^2-\\beta&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nAdd the equations and use the previous results.\n$$\\begin{align*}3(\\alpha^3+\\beta^3)+6(\\alpha^2+\\beta^2)-(\\alpha+\\beta)&=0\\\\3(\\alpha^3+\\beta^3)+6\\left(\\frac{14}{3}\\right)-(-2)&=0\\\\3(\\alpha^3+\\beta^3)&=-30\\\\\\alpha^3+\\beta^3&=-10\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      }
    ]
  },
